-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dir_err_directive_table.adam - Break step of dir_directive_table: a value
  word a directive's row does not hold (SM0100 names the row's two words),
  and a build directive inside a body (PR0008: a body takes only those its
  row lets stand there).
*******************************************************************************/

/*
@@test
  kind error
@@end
*/

module exe dir_err_directive_table;

@subsystem windows; // ERROR SM0100@12: 'windows' is not a value of @subsystem: it takes console | gui
@addverinfo yes; // ERROR SM0100@13: 'yes' is not a value of @addverinfo: it takes on | off

begin
  @outputpath "x"; // ERROR PR0008@3: the build directive '@outputpath' stands only in the directive prologue, right after the module header
end.
